Bundled third-party material
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This section covers material redistributed *inside* this repository, which is the
material that carries an attribution obligation. Runtime dependencies are resolved
from npm by the consumer rather than redistributed here; they are enumerated with
their licences in package-lock.json and checked on every build by
scripts/licence-guard.mjs (see docs/DECISIONS.md, ADR-009).

BPMN 2.0 XML schemas — third_party/omg/
  BPMN20.xsd, Semantic.xsd, BPMNDI.xsd, DI.xsd, DC.xsd
  Published by the Object Management Group (OMG) as part of the BPMN 2.0
  specification: https://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/2.0.2/
  Content is unmodified. Line endings are normalised to LF by .gitattributes.
  BPMN, OMG and the OMG logo are trademarks of the Object Management Group.

  Note: the terms under which OMG machine-readable specification files may be
  redistributed are not clearly stated by OMG, and this question is unresolved
  upstream in the wider open-source community. Recorded as known-unresolved rather
  than assumed settled. These files are used only by the XSD validation gate, so
  the exit — should it be needed — is to fetch them at install time or make schema
  validation opt-in, neither of which changes the product.

BPMN MIWG reference models — bench/corpus/miwg/
  Reference models from the BPMN Model Interchange Working Group at the Object
  Management Group.
  Source:  https://github.com/bpmn-miwg/bpmn-miwg-test-suite
  Licence: Creative Commons Attribution 3.0 Unported (CC BY 3.0)
           https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/
  Content is unmodified. Line endings are normalised to LF by .gitattributes.
  Per-file provenance, including the pinned upstream commit, is recorded in
  bench/corpus/PROVENANCE.md.

